            "<p>Produces bile</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Pancreas</p>",
            "<p>Produces digestive enzymes</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Large Intestine</p>",
            "<p>Water absorption</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1f64wpo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Renal Physiology"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j8zmiy5",
      "content": "The kidneys maintain fluid balance and remove metabolic waste through urine formation."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Memorize normal blood values and vital signs, as direct numerical questions are frequently asked in competitive exams.",
        "Understand the functional mechanics of Renal and Endocrine systems for high-yield scenario-based questions.",
        "Pay special attention to Cardiac and Respiratory physiology principles during final exam revisions."
      ],
      "id": "6oh7wgz"
    },
